  "worked_solution": "Notice that the terms of the corresponding sequence\n\n$$\n7,\\,14,\\,21,\\,…,\\,63,\\,70.\n$$\n\n are multiples of $7,$ and since $70÷7=10,$ there are $10$ terms in total. \n\nTherefore, the $n$th term of the sequence has the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=7n,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ ranges from $n=1$ to $n=10.$ Indeed: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =7(1)=7 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =7(2)=14 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =7(3)=21 \\\\  & \\,\\,⋮ \\\\ {a}_{9} & =7(9)=63 \\\\ {a}_{10} & =7(10)=70\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nS=7+14+21+⋯+63+70={\\sum }_{n=1}^{10}7n.\n$$",
